// The count of Process.read_bytes() must be an integer, and an integer is an
// Int or an integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments). The
// child is /bin/cat, which echoes the bytes, so the Int count reads the same
// two bytes as the Number count. A fractional count is a runtime error that
// halts the program.
// COVERS: integer-arg process-read-bytes
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 30
// CHECK: ab
var p = spawn("/bin/cat", []);
p.write("abcdef");
p.close_stdin();
print p.read_bytes(2i);
p.read_bytes(2.5);
print "unreachable";
